.TH HLSE-SERVER 1 "2026-07-08" "HLSE 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hlse-server \- HLSE HTTP/JSON API and web dashboard server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hlse-server
.RB [ --host
.IR addr ]
.RB [ --port
.IR n ]
.RB [ --webroot
.IR dir ]
.br
.B hlse-server
.RB [ --help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hlse-server
is a small, dependency-free HTTP/1.1 server (POSIX sockets, libc, and
pthreads only \(em no third-party runtime) that exposes the HLSE detection
engine as a JSON API and serves a local, self-contained web dashboard for
scanning URLs, messages, code/config for leaked secrets, and files. It
links the same detection engine the
.BR hlse_core (1)
CLI uses; verdicts are identical.
.PP
The server binds
.B 127.0.0.1
(loopback) by default and performs no authentication. It is a local
developer tool, not a public-facing service: to expose it beyond the local
host, place it behind a reverse proxy that terminates TLS and handles
authentication.
.PP
Each accepted connection is handled on its own detached thread, capped at
64 simultaneous connections. A connection beyond the cap receives an
immediate
.B 503
response with no thread spawned, so a connection burst cannot exhaust
memory or file descriptors.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --host " addr"
Bind address. Default
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.BI --port " n"
Listen port. Default
.BR 8080 .
.TP
.BI --webroot " dir"
Directory containing
.IR index.html ", " app.js ", and " style.css .
Default
.BR ./web .
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show usage and exit.
.SH ENDPOINTS
All API responses are
.BR application/json .
.TP
.B GET /
The web dashboard.
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/health
.nf
{ "status": "ok", "engine": "<version>", "server": "<version>" }
.fi
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/version
.nf
{ "version": "<version>" }
.fi
.TP
.B "POST /api/v1/scan/url"
.RS
Body:
.RS
.nf
{ "url": "<url>" }
.fi
.RE
Scan a URL for phishing/spoofing. Returns
.IR score ", " severity ", " action ", and " reasons .
.RE
.TP
.B "POST /api/v1/scan/text"
.RS
Body:
.RS
.nf
{ "text": "<message>" }
.fi
.RE
Scan a message for scam/phishing language. Same response shape as
.IR /scan/url .
.RE
.TP
.B "POST /api/v1/scan/secrets"
.RS
Body:
.RS
.nf
{ "text": "<code or config>" }
.fi
.RE
Scan code or config text for leaked credentials.
.RE
.TP
.B "POST /api/v1/scan/file"
.RS
Body:
.RS
.nf
{ "filename": "<name>", "content": "<file text>" }
.fi
.RE
Combine name-based masquerade detection with a leaked-secret content scan.
Nothing is written to disk server-side.
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
The server runs until interrupted (SIGINT/SIGTERM) and then exits
.BR 0 .
It exits
.B 1
on a socket error (bind/listen failure) and
.B 2
on a usage error (bad arguments).
.SH EXAMPLES
Start on the default port and open the dashboard at
.UR http://127.0.0.1:8080
.UE :
.RS
.B hlse-server
.RE
.PP
Scan a URL from the command line:
.RS
.nf
curl -s localhost:8080/api/v1/scan/url -d '{"url":"https://paypa1.com"}'
.fi
.RE
.SH PRIVACY
HLSE performs all detection locally. The server makes no outbound network
connections and sends nothing off-host; every verdict is computed by the
same engine the CLI uses.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hlse_core (1).
.I docs/API.md
in the project source for the full endpoint reference.
.PP
Project home and documentation:
.UR https://github.com/shizukutanaka/hlse
.UE
